#
# Counter-example for the native math:ProjectionDroppedParameterization gate: a LOSSY
# math:ProjectionRecord (logic:preservationKind logic:SoundUnderApproximation) projects a
# source math:Distribution that carries a math:distributionParameterization, but the
# record enumerates NO logic:unsupportedConstruct — the parameterization drop is silent.
# The native gate MUST emit math:ProjectionDroppedParameterization (and no other
# projection failure class): a lossy projection declares such a drop as recorded loss
# rather than performing it silently.
# Single violation: the dropped parameterization is not enumerated in logic:unsupportedConstruct.
# The record DOES enumerate an unrelated drop, so math:UndeclaredUnsupportedConstruct — the
# coarser obligation that a lossy record name SOMETHING — is satisfied, and what remains is
# exactly the finer claim under test: the parameterization specifically went unrecorded.
# Back-reference: math:distributionParameterization / math:ProjectionDroppedParameterization (slices/grounding/math/module.ttl).
@prefix math:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:normalDistribution a math:Distribution ;
    math:distributionFamily ex:normalFamily ;
    math:distributionParameterization ex:meanStddev .

ex:normalFamily a math:DistributionFamily .
ex:meanStddev a math:DistributionParameterization .

ex:droppedProjection a math:ProjectionRecord ;
    math:projectionSource ex:normalDistribution ;
    math:projectionTargetName "SciPy stats (family label only)" ;
    logic:preservationKind logic:SoundUnderApproximation ;
    logic:unsupportedConstruct "dropped the declared support bounds" .
